{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--alienable-nouns-kor-relative-clause","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--kor-construction"],"statement":{"en":"Alienable nouns cannot take person marking directly and instead express possession via a pre-head relative clause headed by kor 'have'.","ja":"譲渡可能名詞は人称接辞を直接取ることができず、動詞 kor「持つ」を述語とする名詞修飾関係節によって所有を表す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["kor"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0012-05","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2022@handbook-epub/l0006-14","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--belonging-form-restricted-to-inalienable-shizunai","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--overview"],"statement":{"en":"In Shizunai Ainu, the belonging form of nouns is used exclusively to express inalienable possession.","ja":"静内方言において、名詞の所属形は譲渡不能所有を表すためにのみ用いられる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0017-01","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0074-16","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0154-09","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--ku-bow-affiliative-and-alienable","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--class-membership"],"statement":{"en":"The noun ku 'bow' can take an affiliative form kuwehe due to traditional hunter-weapon worldview, while also permitting alienable kor possession.","ja":"名詞 ku「弓」は伝統的世界観を反映して所属形 kuwehe をとり得るが、通常の譲渡可能道具と同様に kor による所有も可能である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"specific","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["ku","kuwehe"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0226-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"contradicts","claim":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--ku-bow-alienable-only","differs_in":"dialect","note":"Nakagawa documents affiliative kuwehe in Saru trap-bow contexts, whereas Satō states ku never takes affiliative forms."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--ku-bow-alienable-only","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--kor-construction"],"statement":{"en":"The noun ku 'bow' does not take an affiliative form and is possessed only using ku-kor.","ja":"名詞 ku「弓」は所属形をとらず、ku-kor によってのみ所有される。"},"type":"absence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"specific","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["ku","ku-kor ku"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0169-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--affiliative-form-potential-universal-applicability","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--class-membership"],"statement":{"en":"Provided appropriate semantic conditions are met, potentially every common noun can take an affiliative possessive form.","ja":"意味的条件さえ整えば、潜在的にはあらゆる普通名詞が所属形をとり得る。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"tentative","conditions":["appropriate semantic conditions"]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0227-05","stance":"proposes"}],"relations":[{"kind":"contrasts","claim":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--belonging-form-restricted-closed-class-shizunai","differs_in":"framework","note":"Nakagawa analyzes affiliative marking as potentially open to all common nouns depending on construal, whereas Refsing analyzes it as a closed lexical class of about fifty items."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--belonging-form-restricted-closed-class-shizunai","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--class-membership"],"statement":{"en":"In Shizunai Ainu, nouns that can take the belonging form are limited to a small closed class of around fifty items expressing inalienable possession.","ja":"静内方言において所属形をとりうる名詞は譲渡不能所有を表す50語強の限られた語群にすぎない。"},"type":"membership","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0078-13","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--sakhalin-ainu-pervasive-possessed-forms","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--analytical-perspectives"],"statement":{"en":"Unlike Hokkaido Ainu, where some nouns do not take possessed forms for ordinary possession, almost all nouns take possessed forms in Sakhalin Ainu.","ja":"北海道方言とは異なり、樺太アイヌ語ではほぼすべての名詞が通常の所有において所属形をとる。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido","doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"almost all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0108-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--sakhalin-affiliative-form-lexical-hierarchy","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--class-membership"],"statement":{"en":"In Sakhalin Ainu, affiliative forms are standard for body parts and kin terms, frequent for instruments and buildings, but normally absent for natural phenomena and geographical features.","ja":"樺太アイヌ語において所属形は身体部位・親族名称で概ね用いられ、道具・建築物で頻繁に用いられる一方、自然現象や地勢語では通常用いられない。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"most","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:tangiku2022@handbook-epub/l0057-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--sakhalin-ainu-pervasive-possessed-forms","differs_in":"scope","note":"Tangiku articulates the specific lexical hierarchy and limits of affiliative marking in Sakhalin, refining Nakagawa's generalization that almost all nouns take it."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--kotan-affiliative-form-existence","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--affiliative-construction"],"statement":{"en":"The noun kotan 'village' has an affiliative form kotan-u despite not being a body part.","ja":"名詞 kotan「村」は身体部位ではないが所属形 kotan-u を持つ。"},"type":"existence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"specific","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["kotan","kotanu"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0169-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--kotan-dual-construction-frequency","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--class-membership"],"statement":{"en":"The noun kotan 'village' is used in both the concept-form construction and the affiliative-form construction with roughly equal frequency.","ja":"名詞 kotan「村」は概念形構文でも所属形構文でも同程度使われる。"},"type":"frequency","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"specific","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["kotan","kotanu"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0217-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--kotan-affiliative-form-existence","differs_in":null,"note":"Nakagawa specifies that kotan is split roughly equally between affiliative and concept-form possessive constructions."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--bound-body-parts-incompatible-with-kor","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--affiliative-construction"],"statement":{"en":"Bound body-part nouns cannot be possessed via the possessive verb kor.","ja":"拘束身体部位名詞は所有動詞 kor を用いて領属を表すことができない。"},"type":"judgement","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":["bound body-part nouns"]},"forms":["kor","pake","sik"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0297-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--free-counterparts-to-bound-body-parts-permit-kor","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--kor-construction"],"statement":{"en":"Independent free forms corresponding to bound body-part nouns allow possession with kor.","ja":"拘束身体部位名詞に対応する独立形名詞は kor による所有表現が可能である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"specific","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["kor","sapane","sik-nu"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0297-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"contrasts","claim":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--bound-body-parts-incompatible-with-kor","differs_in":"level-of-analysis","note":"Derived or independent counterparts to bound body-part nouns permit kor possession, in contrast to their bound root counterparts."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--inalienable-nouns-in-ainu-chiefly-body-parts-and","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--affiliative-construction"],"statement":{"en":"Inalienable nouns in Ainu, chiefly body parts and kin terms, take direct affixation of possessive affixes.","ja":"主に身体部位や親族呼称からなるアイヌ語の譲渡不能名詞は、所有接辞の直接的な付加を受ける。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0002-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--inalienable-nouns-in-ainu-are-obligatorily-possessed-and","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--affiliative-construction"],"statement":{"en":"Inalienable nouns in Ainu are obligatorily possessed and take head-marked person indexation.","ja":"アイヌ語の譲渡不能名詞は義務的所有名詞であり、主要部標示による人称指標を受ける。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0037-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--the-affiliative-form-possessive-construction-is-used-for","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--affiliative-construction"],"statement":{"en":"The affiliative-form possessive construction is used for inalienable possession, where Noun2 cannot exist without Noun1.","ja":"所属形所有構文は、名詞₁が存在しなければ名詞₂がそもそも存在できないような、いわゆる譲渡不可能な関係を表す場合に用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0215-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--items-of-clothing-and-footwear-that-are-normally","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--affiliative-construction"],"statement":{"en":"Items of clothing and footwear that are normally worn are treated like body parts and expressed in the affiliative form.","ja":"衣類や靴のように通常身に着けているものは、身体名称に準じて所属形で表される。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":["clothing and footwear normally worn"]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0216-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--handheld-tools-and-weapons-that-are-carried-on","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--affiliative-construction"],"statement":{"en":"Handheld tools and weapons that are carried on the person are expressed in the affiliative form, like items of clothing.","ja":"携帯している道具類も、衣類と同様に所属形で表される。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":["tools carried on the person"]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0216-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--part-whole-relations-such-as-spear-handle-cradle","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--affiliative-construction"],"statement":{"en":"Part-whole relations (such as spear handle, cradle strap, or plant seeds) are expressed using the affiliative-form construction.","ja":"全体に対する部分の関係（槍の柄、ゆりかごの紐、草の実など）は所属形構文で表される。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":["part-whole relation"]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0216-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--raw-material-to-product-relationships-such-as-dishes","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--affiliative-construction"],"statement":{"en":"Raw material-to-product relationships (such as dishes or bamboo huts) can be expressed using the affiliative-form construction.","ja":"原料に対する製品の関係（料理の具材や竹で作った家など）は所属形構文で表される。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":["raw material to product relation"]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0217-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--across-dialects-there-is-a-noun-uncise-someone","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--affiliative-construction"],"statement":{"en":"Across dialects, there is a noun uncise 'someone's house' used mainly in verse, which is never used with kor and is always used in the affiliative form.","ja":"cise とは別に諸方言に uncise「〜の家」という名詞があり、主に韻文で用いられ、kor uncise のようには言わず常に所属形で使われる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":["mainly in verse"]},"forms":["uncise"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0218-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--the-noun-kaskamuy-possessing-spirit-guardian-deity-takes","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--affiliative-construction"],"statement":{"en":"The noun kaskamuy 'possessing spirit / guardian deity' takes an affiliative form and undergoes personal inflection just like body-part nouns.","ja":"kaskamuy「憑き神」は身体部位名詞と同じく所属形を取って人称変化する。"},"type":"membership","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["kaskamuy","kaskamuye"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0168-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--in-oral-literature-alongside-the-regular-form-a","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--affiliative-construction"],"statement":{"en":"In oral literature, alongside the regular form a-kotan-u 'my/our village', the construction a-kor kotan-u, which uses both kor and the affiliative form together, is also found.","ja":"口承文芸では a-kotan-u「私の村」のような通常の型に従った形の他に、kor と所属形を併用する a-kor kotan-u という形式もみられる。"},"type":"existence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"exists","modality":"actual","conditions":["in oral literature"]},"forms":["a-kotan-u","a-kor kotan-u"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0169-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--kinship-terms-often-take-affiliative-forms-like-body","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--affiliative-construction"],"statement":{"en":"Kinship terms often take affiliative forms like body parts (e.g. k-unuhu, k-onaha, k-ekasihi, ku-suci, ku-saha, ku-sapo, ku-yupihi, ku-yupo, k-akihi, ku-macirpe, ku-mátaki, ku-poho, ku-matnepoho, ku-mitpoho).","ja":"親族名称は身体部位に準じて所属形を取ることが多い（k-unu-hu「私の母」，k-ona-ha「私の父」，k-ekasi-hi「私の祖父」など）。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["k-unu-hu","k-ona-ha","k-ekasi-hi","ku-suc-i","ku-sa-ha","ku-sapo","ku-yup-ihi","ku-yupo","k-ak-ihi","ku-macirpe","ku-mátak-i","ku-po-ho"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0169-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--in-ainu-alienable-possession-the-verb-have-appears","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--analytical-perspectives"],"statement":{"en":"In Ainu alienable possession, the verb 'have' appears to be the survivor of a formerly larger set of verbs with classificatory functions.","ja":"アイヌ語の譲渡可能所有構文における「持つ」という動詞は、かつて類別詞的機能を持っていたより大きな動詞群の生き残りであると考えられる。"},"type":"diachrony","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0003-01","stance":"proposes"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--in-southern-hokkaido-ainu-the-head-marking-possessive","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--class-membership"],"statement":{"en":"In Southern Hokkaido Ainu, the head-marking possessive construction is restricted to inalienable possession.","ja":"南北海道アイヌ語において、主部標示の所有構文は譲渡不能所有にのみ用いられる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2012@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0011-09","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--definite-possessors-are-most-likely-to-trigger-the","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--class-membership"],"statement":{"en":"Definite possessors are most likely to trigger the morphological possessive construction on the head noun.","ja":"定の所有者は主要部名詞における形態的所所有構文を最も引き起こしやすい。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2012@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0011-10","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--only-inalienable-nouns-typically-body-parts-and-their","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--class-membership"],"statement":{"en":"Only inalienable nouns—typically body parts and their extensions, kinship terms, and relational nouns—can be used in the proper possessive construction.","ja":"譲渡不可能名詞（典型的には身体部位およびその拡張、親族名称、関係名詞）のみが本来的所有構文で用いられる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0009-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--the-noun-mosir-land-world-is-used-only","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--class-membership"],"statement":{"en":"The noun mosir 'land, world' is used only in the concept-form possessive construction in prose, although the affiliative form mosiri occasionally appears in verse.","ja":"mosir「国、世界」は散文では概念形構文でしか使われない（ただし韻文中では所属形 mosiri が現れることがある）。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["mosir","mosiri"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0217-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--in-the-prose-of-saru-chitose-and-horobetsu","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--class-membership"],"statement":{"en":"In the prose of Saru, Chitose, and Horobetsu, cise 'house' never takes the affiliative form in the sense of 'someone's house', but it can do so in verse, and in other dialects it frequently takes the affiliative form even in prose.","ja":"cise「家」は、「誰それの家」という意味において、沙流・千歳・幌別方言の散文では所属形をとらないが、韻文では所属形になることがあり、それ以外の方言では散文でも所属形で表現されることが多い。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":["in the meaning 'someone's house'"]},"forms":["cise","cisehe"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0217-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--almost-all-words-for-parts-of-the-body","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--class-membership"],"statement":{"en":"Almost all words for parts of the body have a belonging form.","ja":"身体部位を表す語のほぼすべてが所属形を持つ。"},"type":"membership","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":["body part nouns"]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0078-14","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--except-in-situations-where-a-body-part-is","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--class-membership"],"statement":{"en":"Except in situations where a body part is mentioned in a general sense, the belonging form will be used for body parts.","ja":"身体部位が一般的な意味で言及される場合を除き、身体部位名詞には所属形が用いられる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":["body part nouns","except when mentioned in a general sense"]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0078-15","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--in-the-category-of-abstract-parts-of-the","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--class-membership"],"statement":{"en":"In the category of abstract parts of the body, only kewtum 'mind, heart, personality', haw 'voice', and ruye 'track, footprints' appear in the Shizunai material.","ja":"抽象的な「身体部位」のグループでは、著者の静内方言資料には kewtum「心、精神、性格」、haw「声」、ruye「足跡」の3例しか現れない。"},"type":"membership","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"measured","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["kewtum","haw","ruye"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0080-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--the-noun-kewtum-does-not-always-appear-in","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--class-membership"],"statement":{"en":"The noun kewtum does not always appear in the belonging form where it might be expected, such that ku kewtum is as acceptable as ku kewtumu(hu).","ja":"名詞 kewtum は所属形が期待される環境でも必ずしも所属形をとらず、ku kewtum は ku kewtumu(hu) と同様に容認される。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":["kewtum","kewtumu","kewtumuhu"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0080-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--the-noun-haw-always-appears-in-the-belonging","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--class-membership"],"statement":{"en":"The noun haw always appears in the belonging form when it is clear to whom the voice belongs.","ja":"名詞 haw は、その声が誰のものであるかが明確な場合には、常に所属形をとる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"necessary","conditions":["when it is clear to whom the voice belongs"]},"forms":["haw"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0080-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--many-kinship-terms-in-the-shizunai-dialect-lack","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--class-membership"],"statement":{"en":"Many kinship terms in the Shizunai dialect lack a belonging form.","ja":"静内方言における多くの親族名称には所属形が存在しない。"},"type":"absence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0080-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--a-few-kinship-terms-can-appear-either-in","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--class-membership"],"statement":{"en":"A few kinship terms can appear either in the belonging form or in construction with an attributive postposition.","ja":"少数の親族名称は、所属形をとるか、連体格後置詞を伴って現れるかのいずれかの選択肢を持つ。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"exists","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0080-07","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--common-nouns-that-inflect-for-person-are-generally","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--class-membership"],"statement":{"en":"Common nouns that inflect for person are generally inalienable entities such as body parts, or items conceptually assimilated to them such as blood, mind/heart, guardian spirit, and clothing.","ja":"人称変化する普通名詞は、一般に身体部位のような譲渡不能なものであることが多く、また血、心、憑き神、衣服など身体部位に準ずると考えられるものも所属形を取って人称変化することが多い。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0168-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--in-southern-hokkaido-ainu-alienable-possession-is-encoded","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--kor-construction"],"statement":{"en":"In Southern Hokkaido Ainu, alienable possession is encoded periphrastically by a relative clause construction using kor 'have' as the predicate with the possessor as the subject, while the possessee remains unmarked.","ja":"南北海道アイヌ語において、譲渡可能所有はkor「持つ」を述語とし所有者を主語とする関係節に基づいた迂言的構文によって表され、被所有物は無標示のままである。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["kor"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2012@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0011-11","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--alienable-nouns-in-ainu-cannot-take-person-markers","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--kor-construction"],"statement":{"en":"Alienable nouns in Ainu cannot take person markers directly.","ja":"アイヌ語の譲渡可能名詞は人称標識を直接取ることができない。"},"type":"absence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"necessary","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0002-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--although-the-kor-relative-clause-possessive-construction-is","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--kor-construction"],"statement":{"en":"Although the kor relative clause possessive construction is grammatically possible with all non-possessible nouns, only 57 such nouns are attested with kor in Tamura's (1991) lexicon.","ja":"文法的にはkor関係節による所有構文はすべての非所有可能名詞に可能であるが、田村（1991）の語彙集で実際にkorとともに用例がみられる名詞は57語にとどまる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"measured","modality":"actual","conditions":["in Tamura (1991) lexicon with examples"]},"forms":["kor"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0013-01","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--the-concept-form-possessive-construction-with-kor-is","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--kor-construction"],"statement":{"en":"The concept-form possessive construction (with kor) is used for alienable possession, where the existence of Noun2 is not contingent on Noun1.","ja":"概念形所有構文（kor を用いる構文）は、名詞₁が存在しなくても名詞₂の存在に影響を与えないような、いわゆる譲渡可能な関係を表す場合に用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["kor"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0215-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--when-the-relationship-is-not-one-of-inalienable","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--kor-construction"],"statement":{"en":"When the relationship is not one of inalienable possession, the genitive is expressed using attributive postpositions.","ja":"関係が譲渡不能所有ではない場合、連体格後置詞を用いて属格が表される。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":[],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":["when the relationship is not inalienable possession"]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0074-18","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--nouns-such-as-k-ne-money-cannot-directly","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--kor-construction"],"statement":{"en":"Nouns such as káne 'money' cannot directly undergo personal inflection by taking personal affixes, but instead require a relative clause with the verb kor 'have' (e.g. ku-kor káne) to express possession.","ja":"káne「お金」のような名詞は直接人称接辞を付けて人称変化させることができず、kor「持つ」という動詞を用いて ku-kor káne のように修飾する必要がある。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":["alienable nouns like káne"]},"forms":["káne","kor","ku-kor káne"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0167-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--some-kinship-terms-do-not-take-affiliative-forms","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--kor-construction"],"statement":{"en":"Some kinship terms do not take affiliative forms and instead use ku-kor, such as ku-kor totto 'my mother' and ku-kor hāpo 'my father'.","ja":"親族名称の中には所属形を取らず ku-kor totto「私のお母さん」や ku-kor hāpo「私のお父さん」のように ku-kor を用いるものもある。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"exists","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ku-kor totto","ku-kor hāpo","totto","hāpo"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0169-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--inalienable-nouns-in-ainu-are-obligatorily-possessed","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Inalienable nouns in Ainu are obligatorily possessed.","ja":"アイヌ語において譲渡不可能名詞は義務的所有名詞である。"},"type":"membership","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0009-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--ainu-has-an-appositive-possessive-construction-for-alienable","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu has an appositive possessive construction for alienable nouns, which are optionally possessed nouns.","ja":"アイヌ語には、任意所属名詞である譲渡可能名詞に対する同格所有構文が存在する。"},"type":"existence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0037-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--ainu-nouns-exhibit-an-alienability-opposition","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu nouns exhibit an alienability opposition.","ja":"アイヌ語の名詞には譲渡可能性の対立が存在する。"},"type":"existence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2022@handbook-epub/l0002-07","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--ainu-nominal-grammar-possesses-bound-inalienable-nouns-and","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu nominal grammar possesses bound inalienable nouns and non-possessible alienable nouns.","ja":"アイヌ語の名詞文法には結合的譲渡不能名詞と所属形を持たない譲渡可能名詞が存在する。"},"type":"existence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2022@handbook-epub/l0006-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--alienable-possession-is-expressed-with-the-pattern-possessor","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Alienable possession is expressed with the pattern [possessor + kor + conceptual form], whereas inalienable possession is expressed with [possessor + affiliative form].","ja":"分離可能所有は［所有者＋kor＋概念形］の型で表されるのに対し、分離不能所有は［所有者＋所属形］の型で表される。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["kor"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2022pos@handbook-epub/l0093-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--general-nouns-that-can-be-inalienably-possessed-may","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--overview"],"statement":{"en":"General nouns that can be inalienably possessed may appear with pronominal affixes to form the belonging form.","ja":"不可譲譲渡可能な普通名詞は、代名詞的接辞を伴って「所属形」を形成し得る。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"possible","conditions":["inalienably possessed"]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0068-09","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--pronominal-prefixes-in-the-nominative-case-may-attach","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Pronominal prefixes in the nominative case may attach to certain general nouns to express inalienable possession.","ja":"主格の人称接頭辞は、不可譲渡的所有を表す際に特定の一般名詞に接続することがある。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"exists","modality":"possible","conditions":["expressing inalienable possession"]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0072-07","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--pronominal-affixes-in-their-nominative-form-can-be","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topics":["topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split","topic:nominal/alienable-inalienable-split--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Pronominal affixes in their nominative form can be prefixed to any noun capable of taking the belonging form, and a short verb phrase may intervene between the prefix and the noun.","ja":"主格形の人称接辞は所属形をとりうる任意の名詞に接頭辞として付加でき、接頭辞と名詞の間に短い動詞句を挿入することが可能である。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"possible","conditions":["nouns capable of taking the belonging form"]},"forms":["ku wen mataki"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0148-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
